  <title>Project 2 Overview</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m00662</md:content-id>
    <md:title>Project 2 Overview</md:title>
    <md:uuid>b763452d-f0ac-4b8c-9983-61abdc5d5d03</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section><para>In this culminating project, you will integrate the ideas from the unit and engage in multiple aspects of mathematical modeling.
</para>

<para>In the first activity, you interpret and analyze given models that represent the constraints and conditions in a situation. In the second activity, you create your own models after specifying quantities of interest, identifying relevant information, and setting the constraints.
</para>

<title>Project Activities</title>
<list type="enumerated">
  <item>Determining a Solution to Inequalities</item>
  <item>Interpret a Set of Mathematical Models</item>
  <item>Perform Mathematical Modeling</item>
</list>


<title>Learning Targets</title>
<para>When you finish this project, you will have demonstrated how to:</para>
<list>
  <item>Interpret inequalities and graphs in a mathematical model.
  </item>
  <item>Choose variables, specify the constraints, and write inequalities to create a mathematical model.
  </item>
</list>
</section>
</content>
</document>
